body:
Daily success emails from `backup-restic` were too noisy, and there was no weekly view resilient to reboots/impermanence. This change replaces per-run notifications with a weekly digest and includes per-path freshness so stale backup sources are obvious.

- **Notification model**
  - Removed per-run `onSuccess` email trigger from `backup-restic`.
  - Added `backup-restic-weekly-digest-email` systemd timer/service (`OnCalendar=weekly`, `Persistent=true`).

- **Reboot-safe digest state**
  - Introduced persistent run log at `/var/lib/backup-restic/runs.log`.
  - Added `StateDirectory = "backup-restic"` to services so digest data survives reboot under existing persisted `/var/lib`.

- **Per-run metadata capture**
  - `backup-restic` now records, per run:
    - timestamp + result
    - restic output tail
    - last-modified info for each backed-up path (`/inaba`, `/GF-01`, `/persist`, `/backups/persists`, `/backups/vps-7de6b7ba`, `/backups/caldav`)
  - Path freshness is derived from restic snapshot metadata using `restic ls --long --recursive ... | tail -n 1` (with a compatibility fallback parser if time-sorting is unavailable), instead of filesystem tree scanning.

- **Weekly digest content**
  - Weekly mail now reports:
    - the **most recent** `backup-restic` run result (success/failure) from the persisted run log
    - recursive modtime for each configured top-level backup path, queried from restic metadata
  - Weekly mail no longer includes restic log tail output.

- **Digest send/clear behavior**
  - Digest log is truncated only after successful SMTP send.
  - Enabled `set -euo pipefail` to ensure `restic | tee` failures are not masked.

```nix
systemd.timers.backup-restic-weekly-digest-email = {
  wantedBy = [ "timers.target" ];
  timerConfig = {
    OnCalendar = "weekly";
    Persistent = "true";
  };
};
```

The browser client could hang on “Fetching bundle” because the configured `cdn.dos.zone` object key no longer exists (404). This updates both runtime and deploy-time bundle sources to a currently valid js-dos DOOM bundle URL.

- **Runtime bundle fallback (`docs/index.html`)**
  - Replaced the stale remote fallback URL used when `./doom.jsdos` is unavailable.
  - Keeps existing local-first behavior intact; only the remote source changed.

- **GitHub Pages asset generation (`.github/workflows/build-and-deploy.yml`)**
  - Updated the workflow `curl` target for `docs/doom.jsdos` to the same valid source.
  - Aligns deployed artifact generation with the runtime fallback URL.

```js
// before
const remoteBundle = "https://cdn.dos.zone/original/2X/9/9ed7eb9c2c441f56656692ed4e736ff7ab423744.jsdos";

// after
const remoteBundle = "https://cdn.dos.zone/custom/dos/doom.jsdos";
```
